observed = "The architecture page calls LayerX a separate C sequencer/consensus domain and explains signed batches, guarantor certificates, delayed checkpoint finality, custody withdrawals and forced exits as the running network lifecycle, including lines 106-124."
expected = "The merged network has one BFT paxd lifecycle, the kernel proposes blocks, and receipts become final when their blocks commit; operators must not deploy a separate sequencer or checkpoint finality service."
proposal = "Rewrite docs/site/docs/overview/unified-network.md runtime and finality sections around paxd block proposal/commit, shared recovery and tenant namespaces. Move the old checkpoint/custody explanation into an explicitly historical reference if retained."
